{
  "is_sufficient": false,
  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The proposed four-way comparison separates the residual from the overall objective change, but does not distinguish CE from the increase to 64 negatives. A matched 64-negative BCE control would strengthen attribution.",
    "Negative sampling is underspecified: replacement, duplicate handling, sharing across positions, and behavior when fewer than 64 eligible items exist. The loader supplies no user IDs, so excluding each user's complete training history requires an explicit training-side mapping or sampler change.",
    "Reproduction requires exact gate bias and projection initialization, embedding scaling, dropout, normalization placement, optimizer settings, loss reduction, and checkpoint selection. A near-zero sigmoid gate can also suppress learning in the residual branch.",
    "Four variants across four datasets require a concrete remaining-budget estimate and completion policy. Matched seeds alone do not ensure matched backbone initialization or minibatches when added parameters and samplers consume random numbers.",
    "Stale-history dominance remains unverified because perturbation probes completed no users. A projected recent-item mean may learn useful transitions, but cannot establish compatibility, complementarity, or reduced ownership redundancy.",
    "Originality is plausibly incremental, but the numerical potential and difficulty ratings are subjective. Validation uncertainty, repeated selection on 800 users, and the required twenty-user full-catalog simulator protocol need explicit treatment."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Clarify the proposed loss and identify a control that separates negative count from objective choice without assuming sampling correction is necessary.",
      "query": "In SASRec sequential recommendation, how do Turning Dross Into Gold Loss, gSASRec generalized BCE, and Correcting the LogQ Correction compare multi-negative BCE with candidate cross-entropy under uniform sampling restricted to each user's training-unseen items? What are the implications of replacement, duplicate negatives, shared negative sets, and uncorrected logits?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Resolve residual implementation details and assess whether a simpler recency model offers comparable benefits.",
      "query": "For SASRec augmented with h_t + sigmoid(g([h_t,r_t])) W r_t, where r_t is a causal five-item masked mean of tied item embeddings, what evidence from TLSRec and related local/global sequential recommenders guides gate initialization, embedding scale, normalization placement, and comparisons with last-item-only or ungated recent-mean residuals?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Improve experimental attribution and uncertainty reporting while preserving the pinned evaluator and fixed training seed.",
      "query": "For sequential recommendation ablations evaluated on a fixed panel of 200 validation users in each of four datasets using HR@10 with 99 unique sampled negatives, what methods address paired user-level uncertainty, repeated validation selection, and factorial interaction analysis when training seed 42 is fixed and experiments share a strict GPU-time budget?"
    }
  ]
}
